# CRT-X87's helper module: both files are almost entirely `// clang-format off` __asm blocks, so
# formatting them is a no-op -- but clang-format's LANGUAGE GUESSER reads the asm's `[operand]` lines
# as Objective-C message sends and then refuses the file ("Configuration file(s) do(es) not support
# Objective-C"), because our .clang-format declares only `Language: Cpp`. The guess is heuristic over
# the whole file, so it flips on an edit as small as adding one helper -- x87.h passes today and
# x87_shapes.h does not, with identical content shapes. Both are listed so the gate cannot become a
# mystery failure later. Their C++ lines were normalised once with --assume-filename=x.cpp.
